       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
       PROGRAM-ID.           TFRTPROC.
       AUTHOR.               RAGLOW/KALMAN.
       DATE-WRITTEN.         MARCH 1993.
      *INSTALLATION.         GOODYEAR TIRE AND RUBBER CO.

      *D* REMARKS.
      *D*     FREIGHT PROCESSING PROGRAM.
      *D*
      *D*     THIS PROGRAM WILL LOAD THE DAPPLFRT AND DTRANS
      *D*     DATA SETS WITH INFORMATION FROM THE TRANSPORTATION
      *D*     INFORMATION SYSTEM (TIS).  TIS SENDS DATA ABOUT THE
      *D*     RATING AND PAYING OF FREIGHT BILLS FOR THE PLANT.
      *D*
      *C* CHANGES.
      *C*
      *C* SEPT 2, 1994    CR KALMAN
      *C* WHEN A RATED RECORD GETS PAID 0 BY THE USER, THE TISPAIDDATE
      *C* DOES NOT GET FILLED IN (BECAUSE TIS REALLY DIDN'T PAY IT).
      *C* IF A SECOND PAYMENT COMES IN THAT MATCHES TO THE RATED INFO
      *C* IN THE RECORD DESCRIBED IN THE FIRST SENTENCE, IT OVERWRITES
      *C* THE PAID 0 INFO WITH THE SECOND PAYMENT INFO. WHAT
      *C* REALLY SHOULD HAPPEN IS THAT THE SECOND PAYMENT SHOULD CAUSE
      *C* A SEPARTE PAID RECORD TO BE CREATED.  TO MAKE SURE THIS
      *C* DOESN'T HAPPEN AGAIN, THE TIS-PAID-DATE AND THE DAPPL-PAID-
      *C* APPLIED-DATE WILL BOTH BE CHECKED. THEY BOTH MUST EQUAL
      *C* SPACES IF THE RECORD IS RATED.
      *C*
      *C* NOV 14, 1996    CA YODER    REQ #96-036
      *C* WHEN A BILL OF LADING WAS RATED UNDER ONE CARRIER BUT WAS
      *C* PAID TO ANOTHER CARRIER (EX: A PARENT COMPANY), THE PAID
      *C* WOULDN'T MATCH UP WITH A RATED, SINCE IT WAS A DIFFERENT
      *C* CARRIER CODE.  THE LOGIC WAS CHANGED IN THIS CASE THAT THE
      *C* RATED AND PAID CARRIERS ON A FREIGHT RECORD WERE DIFFERENT.
      *C* IF NO MATCH IS FOUND AGAINST THE PAID CARRIER, THE RATED
      *C* CARRIER IS THEN CHECKED ONLY IN THIS SITUATION.  THIS WAY,
      *C* THE PLANT WILL NOT HAVE TO RECONCILE BY HAND.
      *C*
      *C* MAY 13, 2004    CA YODER
      *C*  INCREASED SIZE OF RELATIVE REC # FIELD AFTER LAWTON'S
      *C*  FREIGHT FILE EXCEEDED 9999 RECORDS.
      *C*

       ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.
       CONFIGURATION SECTION.
       SPECIAL-NAMES.    I-O-FEEDBACK IS I-O-FEEDBACK-AREA.

      ******************************************************************
       INPUT-OUTPUT SECTION.
      ******************************************************************
       FILE-CONTROL.
           SELECT DAPPLFRT-SEQ-O
                  ASSIGN TO DATABASE-MCFPCA1100
                  ORGANIZATION IS SEQUENTIAL
                  ACCESS MODE IS SEQUENTIAL
                  FILE STATUS IS FILE-STATUS.
           SELECT DAPPLFRT-RRN-O
                  ASSIGN TO DATABASE-MCFPCA1100
                  ORGANIZATION IS RELATIVE
                  ACCESS MODE IS DYNAMIC
                  RELATIVE KEY IS DAPPLFRT-RRN
                  FILE STATUS IS FILE-STATUS.
           SELECT DAPPLFRT-PO-I
                  ASSIGN TO DATABASE-MCFLCA1101
                  ORGANIZATION IS INDEXED
                  ACCESS MODE IS DYNAMIC
                  RECORD KEY IS EXTERNALLY-DESCRIBED-KEY
                  WITH DUPLICATES
                  FILE STATUS IS FILE-STATUS.
           SELECT DAPPLFRT-CAR-I
                  ASSIGN TO DATABASE-MCFLCA1102
                  ORGANIZATION IS INDEXED
                  ACCESS MODE IS DYNAMIC
                  RECORD KEY IS EXTERNALLY-DESCRIBED-KEY
                  WITH DUPLICATES
                  FILE STATUS IS FILE-STATUS.
           SELECT DAPPLFRT-PCP-I
                  ASSIGN TO DATABASE-MCFLCA1103
                  ORGANIZATION IS INDEXED
                  ACCESS MODE IS DYNAMIC
                  RECORD KEY IS EXTERNALLY-DESCRIBED-KEY
                  WITH DUPLICATES
                  FILE STATUS IS FILE-STATUS.
           SELECT DAPPLFRT-RCP-I
                  ASSIGN TO DATABASE-MCFLCA1104
                  ORGANIZATION IS INDEXED
                  ACCESS MODE IS DYNAMIC
                  RECORD KEY IS EXTERNALLY-DESCRIBED-KEY
                  WITH DUPLICATES
                  FILE STATUS IS FILE-STATUS.
           SELECT DAPPLFRT-VS-I
                  ASSIGN TO DATABASE-MCFLCA1105
                  ORGANIZATION IS INDEXED
                  ACCESS MODE IS DYNAMIC
                  RECORD KEY IS EXTERNALLY-DESCRIBED-KEY
                  WITH DUPLICATES
                  FILE STATUS IS FILE-STATUS.
           SELECT ERROR-O
                  ASSIGN TO DATABASE-FRTERRFL
                  ORGANIZATION IS SEQUENTIAL
                  ACCESS MODE IS SEQUENTIAL
                  FILE STATUS IS FILE-STATUS.
           SELECT FREIGHT-I
                  ASSIGN TO DATABASE-FRTDUMMY.
           SELECT HOLDFRT-O
                  ASSIGN TO DATABASE-HOLDDUMMY
                  ORGANIZATION IS SEQUENTIAL
                  ACCESS MODE IS SEQUENTIAL
                  FILE STATUS IS FILE-STATUS.
           SELECT MACCOUNT-INFO-O
                  ASSIGN TO DATABASE-MCFLCA0101
                  ORGANIZATION IS INDEXED
                  ACCESS MODE IS DYNAMIC
                  RECORD KEY IS EXTERNALLY-DESCRIBED-KEY
                  FILE STATUS IS FILE-STATUS.

      ******************************************************************
       DATA DIVISION.
      ******************************************************************

       FILE SECTION.

       FD  DAPPLFRT-SEQ-O
           LABEL RECORDS ARE STANDARD.
       01  DAPPLFRT-SEQ-REC-O.
           COPY DDS-MCRPCA1100  OF MCFPCA1100.

       FD  DAPPLFRT-RRN-O
           LABEL RECORDS ARE STANDARD.
       01  DAPPLFRT-RRN-REC-O.
           COPY DDS-MCRPCA1100  OF MCFPCA1100.

       FD  DAPPLFRT-PO-I
           LABEL RECORDS ARE STANDARD.
       01  DAPPLFRT-PO-REC-I.
           COPY DDS-MCRPCA1100  OF MCFLCA1101.

       FD  DAPPLFRT-CAR-I
           LABEL RECORDS ARE STANDARD.
       01  DAPPLFRT-CAR-REC-I.
           COPY DDS-MCRPCA1100  OF MCFLCA1102.

       FD  DAPPLFRT-PCP-I
           LABEL RECORDS ARE STANDARD.
       01  DAPPLFRT-PCP-REC-I.
           COPY DDS-MCRPCA1100  OF MCFLCA1103.

       FD  DAPPLFRT-RCP-I
           LABEL RECORDS ARE STANDARD.
       01  DAPPLFRT-RCP-REC-I.
           COPY DDS-MCRPCA1100  OF MCFLCA1104.

       FD  DAPPLFRT-VS-I
           LABEL RECORDS ARE STANDARD.
       01  DAPPLFRT-VS-REC-I.
           COPY DDS-MCRPCA1100  OF MCFLCA1105.

       FD  ERROR-O.
       01  ERROR-REC-O                PIC X(191).

       FD  FREIGHT-I
           DATA RECORD IS FREIGHT-REC-I
           RECORD CONTAINS 133 CHARACTERS
           LABEL RECORDS ARE STANDARD.
       01  FREIGHT-REC-I              PIC X(133).

       FD  HOLDFRT-O.
       01  HOLDFRT-REC-O              PIC X(133).

       FD  MACCOUNT-INFO-O
           LABEL RECORDS ARE STANDARD.
       01  MACCOUNT-INFO-REC-O.
           COPY DDS-MCRPCA0100  OF MCFLCA0101.

